<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ynglings</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as House of Yngling, Yngling dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ynglings were a legendary dynasty of Swedish kings at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uppsala">Uppsala</a>, said to descend from the god Freyr. Their history is told in the poem Ynglingatal and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/snorri-sturluson">Snorri Sturluson</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ynglinga-saga">Ynglinga saga</a> of the 13th century. Medieval Norwegian kings claimed descent from them, but most of the early kings cannot be confirmed as historical.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ynglings.jpg" alt="Ynglings" width="320" height="263" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hugo Hamilton (1802–1871) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Konung_Ingjald_Illr%C3%A5da_br%C3%A4nner_upp_6_Fylkiskonungar_by_Hugo_Hamilton.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
